Pursuant to Article 38 of the National Assembly Act, the fixed numbers of members of the Standing Committees of the National Assembly shall be as follows: <Amended on June 10, 2020; October 26, 2025; and July 30, 2026.>
1. House Steering Committee: 28 members;
2. Legislation and Judiciary Committee: 18 members;
3. Political Affairs Committee: 24 members;
4. Finance, Economy and Planning Committee: 22 members;
5. Education Committee: 16 members;
6. Science, ICT, Broadcasting and Communications Committee: 20 members;
7. Foreign Affairs and Unification Committee: 21 members;
8. National Defense Committee: 17 members;
9. Public Administration and Security Committee: 22 members;
10. Culture, Sports and Tourism Committee: 16 members;
11. Agriculture, Food, Rural Affairs, Oceans and Fisheries Committee: 19 members;
12. Trade, Industry, Energy, SMEs and Startups Committee: 24 members;
13. Health and Welfare Committee: 24 members;
14. Climate, Energy, Environment and Labor Committee: 26 members;
15. Land, Infrastructure and Transport Committee: 30 members;
16. Intelligence Committee: 12 members;
17. Gender Equality and Family Committee: 17 members.
